  "observations": [
    "Published async initialize prepares session/widgets and sends no automatic page.viewed. Explicit track once per view; browser response precedes full asynchronous validation.",
    "Authenticated attribution/events validates before received but still queues tracking; received has no event ID or completion promise. Session/profile must already agree; business scopes identifiers.",
    "Action definition is separate from occurrences; custom name normalized and action must exist. Manual custom event requires object, whereas Custom API can omit it; present object requires matching blueprint/object_type.",
    "Object creation and inline entity setup may occur before tracking; received is not proof of every desired result or a universally deduplicated event.",
    "Unix seconds or ISO timestamp, amount/currency and inherited object amount are distinct from reporting conversion/attribution. Cart quantity is resulting quantity, not change amount.",
    "Source origin is recorded in caller bookkeeping and supported session/URL context; not a universal invented source event field. Subscription event is not proof of customer consent/sendability.",
    "Existing safe catalog/manual sources are approved P3 2x. No DB, UI, API, SDK execution, fixture, consent, token, event, send or worker action.",
    "Published track returns the SDK Response wrapper: failed/succeeded/json(), not native fetch ok/status. This was corrected during local source audit before any commit/publication, then rebuilt and rechecked visually.",
    "Omitted tracked_at falls back to Time.current in EventTracker at processing, not a guaranteed HTTP receipt timestamp; article states recording time and requires original timestamp for delayed events."
  ],
  "method": "Read-only source and published npm/CDN inspection; code snippets checked for syntax only."
